Subject: [PATCH] Preserve Safari reverse channel after PTTH upgrade

Mark the upgraded connection as reverse before reading acknowledgements. The
staging prefix still belongs to the original POST /reverse, so sniffing that
prefix cannot identify a subsequent HTTP 200. Reverse ACKs are deliberately
drained without dispatch; HLS FCUP payloads arrive separately through /action.
Reset staging on completed forward requests so keep-alive requests are sniffed
using their own prefix. No acknowledgement body is accumulated.

--- a/lib/httpd.c
+++ b/lib/httpd.c
@@ -587 +587,3 @@
-                    http_request_is_reverse(connection->request);
+                    /* After /reverse, all incoming bytes are acknowledgements,
+                     * not requests. Staging still contains the POST's prefix. */
+                    http_request_set_reverse(connection->request);
@@ -703,0 +706,2 @@
+                connection->staging_len = 0;
+                connection->staging[0] = '\0';
